course: dictionary
lesson: 5112
title: The long tube inside you
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your intestines are long tubes in your belly, and food travels through them after it leaves your stomach. When you meet a new word, read the words around it. «In the small intestine, a tube about six metres long folded up in your belly, the food is broken down fully and passes into the blood.» Tube, belly and food tell you that an intestine is a body part that food moves through.
explain: The two parts do different jobs. The small intestine takes the useful parts of food into the blood. The large intestine takes water back from what is left and pushes out waste as poo. «Fibre from fruit, vegetables and whole grains helps food move through the intestines.» Fibre helps food move along, so the intestines are the path that food takes.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Food takes a long journey: the stomach churns it, then the small intestine soaks it into the blood.» Does "intestine" fit there? Yes, it is the part of the journey after the stomach. If you are still unsure, a dictionary or a science book will settle it.
fact: The intestines are long tubes in your belly that food passes through after the stomach.
fact: The small intestine takes the useful parts of food into the blood.
fact: The large intestine takes water back and pushes out waste as poo.
fact: «The small intestine of an adult is about six metres (about 20 feet) long.»
fact: Food goes mouth, oesophagus (food pipe), stomach, small intestine, large intestine.
exercise: «The small intestine takes the useful parts of food into the blood.» Where do the useful parts of food go? | Into the bin | *Into the blood | Up into the mouth | Out as poo
exercise: «The large intestine takes water back from what is left.» What does the large intestine do with water? | It throws water out of the mouth | It stores water in the stomach | *It takes water back | It turns water into food
exercise: In the order food travels, what comes after the stomach? | The mouth | The oesophagus | *The small intestine | The large intestine
test: Which part of the intestines pushes out waste as poo? | *The large intestine | The stomach | The small intestine | The mouth
test: Roughly how long is the small intestine of an adult? | About 60 centimetres | *About 6 metres | About 1 metre | About 60 metres
exam: «Fibre from fruit, vegetables and whole grains helps food move through the intestines.» What does fibre do? | Turns food into blood | Stops food reaching the stomach | *Helps food move through the intestines | Makes you grow taller
